Here’s the fastest way to run it locally on Windows.
Prereqs
MongoDB running (local or cloud)
Node.js 18+ and Python 3.10+
Chrome (to load the extension)
API keys: GEMINI_API_KEY; optional: HF_TOKEN (for diarization)
1) Configure environment
Create backend/.env:
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/meetgist
Create worker/.env:
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/meetgistGEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_KEYHF_TOKEN=YOUR_HF_TOKEN   # optionalUSE_GPU=false            # set true only if you have CUDA
2) Install dependencies
Backend:
cd "E:\PROJECTS\Meeting Summarizer\Meetgist\backend"npm install
Worker (Python):
cd "E:\PROJECTS\Meeting Summarizer\Meetgist\worker"python -m venv .venv. .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1pip install --upgrade pippip install -r requirements.txt
3) Build the popup UI (once)
cd "E:\PROJECTS\Meeting Summarizer\Meetgist\extension\react-pop"npm installnpm run build
This generates extension/popup/ used by the Chrome extension.
4) Start the backend API
cd "E:\PROJECTS\Meeting Summarizer\Meetgist\backend"node server.js
Server runs at http://localhost:5000
5) Load the Chrome extension
Open Chrome → navigate to chrome://extensions
Toggle “Developer mode” on
Click “Load unpacked” and select: E:\PROJECTS\Meeting Summarizer\Meetgist\extension
6) Use it
Join a Google Meet. The extension auto-detects the meeting, collects captions, records audio (permission prompt), and on exit uploads to the backend.
Open the extension popup to view the latest summary after processing completes.
Optional: test endpoints without Meet
Transcript-only:
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/saveTranscript `  -H "Content-Type: application/json" `  -d "{""transcript"":""This is a test meeting transcript."",""source"":""test"",""date"":""2025-11-11T10:00:00Z""}"
Multi-modal (with audio file):
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/saveMeeting ^  -F "transcript=Test transcript with audio" ^  -F "title=Test Meeting" ^  -F "date=2025-11-11T10:00:00Z" ^  -F "audio=@C:\path\to\audio.webm" ^  http://localhost:5000/api/saveMeeting
Notes
First run of WhisperX/SentenceTransformers may download models (large).
If you don’t need diarization, omit HF_TOKEN.
On GPU systems, install the correct PyTorch CUDA build and set USE_GPU=true.
All tasks for setup and run are complete.
